S-1 — The clerk opens the enrolment screen
  [The clerk] opens the enrolment screen and sees an entry for each of the four: family name, given names, date of birth and school, the school chosen from the data's 3 schools.
  [The registry] offers enrolment as the only thing the clerk's screens offer; there is no screen for looking learners up.
  [Screen] SC-1, the enrolment screen.
    <brief:11> 11: One goal: **enrol a learner.** A school clerk enters a child's family name, given names, date of birth and school. The registry searches for the child first:
    <R-02> 32: **Cites:** U-07, brief line 11
    <R-02> 34: > One goal: **enrol a learner.**
    <R-02> 36: **Requirement.** The prototype has one goal: to enrol a learner.
    <R-02> 38: **Test.**
    <R-02> 39: - *Set up:* the prototype started and its data reset.
    <R-02> 40: - *Do:* by a windowless check, list every goal the prototype offers the clerk on its screens (what counts as a goal: gap G-08).
    <R-02> 41: - *See:* **Expected:** one goal, enrolling a learner. Pass if the list holds that goal and no other.
    <R-03> 45: **Cites:** U-08, brief line 11
    <R-03> 47: > A school clerk enters a child's family name, given names, date of birth and school.
    <R-03> 49: **Requirement.** To enrol a child, the school clerk enters the child's family name, given names, date of birth and school.
    <R-03> 51: **Test.**
    <R-03> 52: - *Set up:* the prototype started and its data reset.
    <R-03> 53: - *Do:* by a windowless check, open the enrolment screen; enter F, G, D and S for a child the registry does not yet hold (the form of a date and of a school: gap G-07); submit.
    <R-03> 54: - *See:* the screen offers an entry for each of the four — family name, given names, date of birth, school — and the record saved holds F, G, D and S as entered. Pass if all four entries are offered and all four values are saved.
    <ruling:G-07> 32: | G-07 | Date as YYYY-MM-DD; school chosen from the three; all four entered before the search |
    <ruling:G-07> 254: **Recommendation — a proposal for the owner's ruling, not a decision.** We recommend Position A: the date entered as YYYY-MM-DD and refused otherwise, the school chosen from the data's three, and all four entered before the search runs, the school not searched on.
