====================================================================================================
S-4 — The registry searches for the child first
  [The clerk] no act of the clerk's is given at this step.
  [The registry] searches after the clerk has entered all four, and first, before it does anything else with the entry and before any write (against S-3, gap 7); it looks among learners only; it compares the family name, the given names and the date of birth; two values that differ in capitals only are the same, and every difference but capitals makes two values differ; it does not compare the school, which is entered and saved and never searched on, nor any field but the three; it does not read the key table. If it finds exactly one learner the goal goes on at S-5; if it finds none, at S-6; on more than one, at F-4.
  [Screen] none of its own; the search runs between SC-1 and the screen of S-7.
    <brief:11> 11: One goal: **enrol a learner.** A school clerk enters a child's family name, given names, date of birth and school. The registry searches for the child first:
    <brief:13> 13: - if it finds exactly one learner with the same family name, given names and date of birth (capitals ignored), it shows that learner and enters nothing new;
    <brief:14> 14: - if it finds none, it gives the child a new learner number and saves the record;
    <R-04> 58: **Cites:** U-09, brief line 11
    <R-04> 60: > The registry searches for the child first:
    <R-04> 62: **Requirement.** When the clerk has entered the child, the registry searches for the child before it does anything else with the entry.
    <R-04> 64: **Test.**
    <R-04> 65: - *Set up:* the prototype started and its data reset; a program records, in order, every read and every write the registry makes on its data during an enrolment.
    <R-04> 66: - *Do:* enrol a child the registry does not hold (F, G, D, S); then enrol the same child again with the same entries.
    <R-04> 67: - *See:* in each enrolment the search is the first act on the data, before any write; in the second enrolment there is no write. Pass if a search precedes every write in both, and the second has none.
