    <R-05> 79: - *Do:* (a) enrol a child with exactly F, G and D; (b) enrol a child with F and G written in other capitals — for example every letter a capital — and the same D.
    <R-05> 80: - *See:* in (a) and in (b), the screen shows the learner saved in the set-up, with its learner number, and the number of learners is unchanged. **Expected:** learners added: 0 in each of (a) and (b). Pass if both hold. (What the registry does when the search finds more than one: gap G-02.)
    <R-07> 97: **Cites:** U-12, brief line 15
    <R-07> 99: > the clerk sees which of the two happened.
    <R-07> 101: **Requirement.** After the search, the clerk sees which of the two happened: an existing learner was found and shown, or a new learner number was given and the record saved.
    <R-07> 103: **Test.**
