F-4 — More than one learner found
  [At step] S-4.
  [What sets it off] the search of S-4 finds more than one learner. Under the data's settings it is never reached: no two different children share all three fields, and "share" ignores capitals.
  [What the clerk sees] SC-5: the entry is refused, and the registry says the entry cannot be completed.
  [What is saved] nothing new.
    <ruling:G-02> 27: | G-02 | Never reached under the data's settings; if it is, enter nothing new and refuse the entry |
    <ruling:G-02> 102: **Recommendation — a proposal for the owner's ruling, not a decision.** We recommend Position B: under the settings given to both the case is never met, and if it is met the registry enters nothing new and says the entry cannot be completed.
